```go
} else if strings.Contains(item, "@") && !strings.HasPrefix(item, "http://") {
```

This is treating anything with "@" as a file upload. But `email=john@example.org` is body data, not a file upload. File uploads have the format `key@/path/file`, so I need to check if the "@" comes AFTER an "=" sign:

